1
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:08,800
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:09,270 --> 00:02:21,970
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:23,620
Oh Kayıs!

4
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:28,140
Do you testify...

5
00:02:28,420 --> 00:02:32,900
... that I fulfilled my task properly?

6
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:35,220
Yes, our Bey!

7
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,060
Oh Kayıs!

8
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:46,100
Do you accept...

9
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:48,100
... my title as a Bey?

10
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:50,100
Yes, our Bey!

11
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:51,260
Yes, my Bey.

12
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:59,020
If I announce my successor now...

13
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:09,660
... will you accept him like you have
accepted me?

14
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:15,140
And obey his every command?

15
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:17,460
We will, our Bey!

16
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:20,340
We will, our Bey.

17
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:42,740
My successor...

18
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:49,580
... to whom shall I leave my title
faithfully.

19
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:56,300
Your new Kayı Bey...

20
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:05,660
... who will fight in the path of Allah...

21
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:10,980
... who will carry the flag of Kayı from
victories to victories...

22
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:17,700
... who will never accept bondage...

23
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:26,220
... my son...

24
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:03,100
-My Bey!
-Father!

25
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:06,940
Father!

26
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:10,660
Father!

27
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:13,460
Father!

28
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:20,620
Father!

29
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,720
ONE DAY AGO

30
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:43,820
I don't think that way.

31
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:49,460
Because Osman and Yalvak Arslan left to
raid a base of Geyhatu.

32
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:51,940
They won't make it alive for sure.

33
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:59,100
Also, if the poison I sent to Kayı Bey
worked, it means the Tent is now derelict.

34
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:02,620
So there is chaos in the Tent right now.

35
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:06,060
Yes.

36
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:08,420
Yes, for sure there is.

37
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:11,740
I like cleaning.

38
00:06:16,020 --> 00:06:20,500
Once the news comes, we will attack them
from every corner.

39
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:27,260
Are we going to attack Kulacahisar?

40
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:30,220
Are you really asking that?

41
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:32,140
Let me tell you something.

42
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:37,340
How long Kulacahisar resist when I kill
every Kayı?

43
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:38,380
Huh?

44
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,100
You're not underestimating my mind, right?

45
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:55,780
All we need to think about right now is
the raid of Tent.

46
00:06:57,580 --> 00:07:01,980
We need to attack without thinking about
the amount of soldiers we might lose.

47
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:06,260
We won't leave any single Kayı alive!

48
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:09,780
It means we will butcher them all.

49
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:16,100
There you are!

50
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,460
Come here!

51
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:19,860
Come and give the good news!

52
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:25,020
Osman...

53
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:26,460
Osman?

54
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,620
... has returned to Kayı Tent with
his Alp.

55
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:37,700
Osman?

56
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:39,660
He returned where?

57
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:43,260
To Kayı Tent, sir.

58
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:55,820
Perfect!

59
00:07:57,420 --> 00:08:00,380
Didn't he leave to raid the base of
Geyhatu?

60
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:03,540
How did he make it alive from there?

61
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:07,460
Yalvak Arslan?

62
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:11,460
He is alive as well, sir.

63
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:13,500
He is also on his way to Tent.

64
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,260
Knell down.

65
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:28,860
Knell down!

66
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:35,940
Geyhatu.

67
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,059
His base.

68
00:08:37,059 --> 00:08:38,059
Raid.

69
00:08:38,419 --> 00:08:39,380
Osman.

70
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:41,460
Okay.

71
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:44,300
Alright! Shut up!

72
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:46,140
Shut your mouth!

73
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:50,140
Alright.

74
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:51,700
Alright!

75
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:53,380
Shut up already!

76
00:08:53,380 --> 00:08:55,220
Okay.

77
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:59,660
Geyhatu must have left before they even
went there.

78
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:01,780
Yes.

79
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:03,780
Geyhatu left before them.

80
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:08,620
The job fell to our lot, Flatyos.

81
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,540
The job fell to our lot.

82
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:13,340
Osman didn't die.

83
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:17,220
Instead, he returned to the Tent.

84
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:22,260
So, it means when we raid the Tent...

85
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:28,540
... Osman is going to greet us.

86
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:31,420
Well...

87
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:37,140
... if the poison I gave to Targun had
worked...

88
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:40,140
... so if their Kayı Bey died...

89
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:42,420
... there will still be chaos at the Tent.

90
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,860
There will be, right?

91
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:46,980
I'm sure they will blame Osman for
everything.

92
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:48,620
They will, right?

93
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:55,980
Naturaly...

94
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:01,780
... Mighty Caesar says that he doesn't
know Targun.

95
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:05,260
Anyways, my beloved friend...

96
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:09,420
... we will visit Targun and learn it
ourselves.

97
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:15,940
Let's see if their Kayı Bey is still
alive like Osman...

98
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:21,420
... or he is dead as to the poison.

99
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:27,060
What's my duty, Nikola?

100
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:29,300
Your duty?

101
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:33,740
You will prepare yourself, Flatyos.

102
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:41,140
I have a feeling in my guts that we will
take place in a bloody war today.

103
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,380
Do you mean this?

104
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:54,380
It's just a statue, Flatyos.

105
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:55,940
It can't talk.

106
00:11:13,420 --> 00:11:14,460
Father.

107
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:24,060
Thanks to my Rab.

108
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:29,820
After seeing you like this, I will never
complain about something.

109
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:35,900
Inshallah, things are going to get better,
Selcen Hatun.

110
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:42,340
Thanks to my Rab.

111
00:12:42,620 --> 00:12:44,260
Hatuns!

112
00:12:44,780 --> 00:12:45,860
Let's leave.

113
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:48,540
Perhaps, Beys have things to talk about.

114
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:09,540
Bamsı.

115
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:11,260
My Bey.

116
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:18,100
I knew what you were up to all along.

117
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:20,620
Brother.

118
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:23,180
You...

119
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:26,340
... you were unconscious.

120
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:32,020
A Bey never leaves his Tent before he
hands the fiduciary.

121
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,420
Mind and heart work together.

122
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,780
And heart works for the best of people.

123
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:46,860
I heard everything and things happened
in the way I predicted them to.

124
00:13:57,820 --> 00:14:01,340
So, after all, you want to become the Bey.

125
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:07,540
You might want to...

126
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:12,460
... but why would Allah want you to become
the Bey?

127
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:19,420
Dündar Bey.

128
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:22,740
What could Allah want from a Bey?

129
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:27,500
To continue his laws, my Bey.

130
00:14:28,140 --> 00:14:29,260
You are right.

131
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:33,980
After all, Beyhood is supported by
Allah's laws.

132
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:40,980
Tell me, Gündüz.

133
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:42,740
Who preserves the Laws?

134
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:46,020
The Bey who gets his title from Allah.

135
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:48,500
Yes indeed.

136
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:56,700
The better the Laws are preserved,
the better a Bey's administration will be.

137
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:04,580
Now, it's your turn Savcı.

138
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:09,220
What happens when the Laws are spoiled.

139
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:12,300
There will be no unity in the universe,
my Bey.

140
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:14,660
It's the Laws what sustain the sky.

141
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:17,140
It's true.

142
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:22,380
Now, tell me, Osman.

143
00:15:24,220 --> 00:15:29,020
How can the administration be handed from
one Bey to another?

144
00:15:31,220 --> 00:15:34,900
The Bey is the Sun of Laws.

145
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:42,820
And a son of the Bey is a moon enlightened
by that very sun.

146
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,420
Oh, the Sun of Kayıs!

147
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:52,060
Whomever your light enlightens...

148
00:15:53,140 --> 00:15:59,620
... and forms a full moon with your
light...

149
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:03,820
... will be the successor of you.

150
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:11,860
This is how your administration...

151
00:16:14,060 --> 00:16:15,900
... gets handed to your successor.

152
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:20,380
It's true.

153
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:28,180
This is exactly how the administration
changes from one Bey to another.

154
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:34,940
My sons and my brother shall excuse us
now.

155
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:40,420
I need to consult my comrades.

156
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:46,260
In the meantime, you can think of an
explanation.

157
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:20,180
Who shall be the new Bey of Kayıs?

158
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:42,260
My son.

159
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:52,660
Targun Hatun.

160
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:55,460
Tell me whatever you need to tell here.

161
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:08,820
Go on.

162
00:18:09,780 --> 00:18:11,420
The poison Nikola gave me...

163
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:18,860
... with this he asked me to poison the
Beys of Kayı.

164
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:21,100
What are you talking about?

165
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,820
Of course, I wasn't going to.

166
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:26,860
But he wants to meet me in order to learn
whether I did or not.

167
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:31,940
What did you just say?

168
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:35,020
May you stop, aunt.

169
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:38,180
Bala.

170
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,460
Nikola, huh?

171
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:04,940
It's unfair to keep Nikola waiting.

172
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:13,980
You shall go to him now.

173
00:19:15,580 --> 00:19:20,860
Tell him you couldn't poison the Beys of
Kayı and that you have better plan.

174
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:32,700
Listen to me carefully.

175
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:45,660
It's clear what he is talking about with
Bamsı and Abdurrahman Bey.

176
00:19:49,420 --> 00:19:50,620
Yes, it is.

177
00:19:52,980 --> 00:19:57,980
He will consult them and his comrades
about the new Bey of Kayı.

178
00:20:01,660 --> 00:20:03,780
And their choice is obvious.

179
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:11,740
It's also clear who you want, right
brother?

180
00:20:14,060 --> 00:20:15,060
Yes, it is.

181
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:18,100
It's very clear.

182
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:26,020
What are you up to this time, Osman?

183
00:20:27,180 --> 00:20:29,540
There is always something to do, brother.

184
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:36,260
Do I have your permission, my Bey?

185
00:20:36,300 --> 00:20:37,420
Come in.

186
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:45,140
My Bey is waiting for you.

187
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:22,300
The day of salvation is close, father.

188
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:26,100
You will become free once again.

189
00:21:27,140 --> 00:21:29,500
Then, we will take our revenge from
everyone.

190
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:31,860
And Osman will be mine.

191
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:48,500
Let' go!

192
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:58,260
Did you raid the base of Geyhatu
with Yalvak Arslan?

193
00:22:02,220 --> 00:22:03,540
Yes, father.

194
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:06,540
It's true.

195
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:13,300
We thought it'd be better to attack before
they drew their swords against Turks.

196
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:20,820
And then?

197
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:25,180
He wasn't there.

198
00:22:26,900 --> 00:22:28,940
We killed his soldiers and left.

199
00:22:34,780 --> 00:22:39,380
Geyhatu once came to our Tent, my Bey.
And he might again.

200
00:22:39,980 --> 00:22:45,860
Maintaining peace with Geyhatu is similar
to being friends with a bear.

201
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:55,340
And my Osman went to the inn of that bear
to kill it.

202
00:22:57,740 --> 00:23:00,380
However, the bear wasn't there.

203
00:23:01,740 --> 00:23:03,940
How about Yalvak Arslan?

204
00:23:05,740 --> 00:23:10,900
How can you still trust him after
everything he has done?

205
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:18,380
I wasn't tricked by his pledges like the
others.

206
00:23:24,620 --> 00:23:27,540
I looked him in the eyes...

207
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:33,740
... and saw the hopes about the future of
all Turks.

208
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:38,900
My nephew.

209
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:44,140
You are the one who told us not to
believe him.

210
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:48,420
How could you believe him by looking
him in the eyes?

211
00:23:49,100 --> 00:23:50,020
Huh?

212
00:23:51,940 --> 00:23:54,660
What kind of an assurance is this?

213
00:23:56,260 --> 00:23:57,580
Uncle!

214
00:23:58,860 --> 00:24:01,140
It's our own benefits that entrap us.

215
00:24:05,660 --> 00:24:11,020
No one can trick someone who doesn't have
anything to lose.

216
00:24:20,420 --> 00:24:23,180
Now, tell us, Savcı.

217
00:24:25,180 --> 00:24:28,300
What's up with you and Osman?

218
00:24:34,180 --> 00:24:36,060
You made me the Head Alp, my Bey.

219
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:40,500
Yet, he never acknowledged this choice of
yours.

220
00:24:44,660 --> 00:24:46,780
He never thought of me as the Head Alp.

221
00:24:47,740 --> 00:24:52,180
He thinks we are too eager to be trapped.

222
00:24:54,780 --> 00:24:58,540
He thinks that we are slaves who don't
want to be free.

223
00:24:59,180 --> 00:25:03,060
And he goes after an impossible autonomy.

224
00:25:08,500 --> 00:25:10,740
Do you have anything to add, brother?

225
00:25:12,140 --> 00:25:14,580
Isn't there a hope for autonomy?

226
00:25:16,780 --> 00:25:23,660
Those who made us and Mongols enemies
are the ones who lost at Kösedağ war.

227
00:25:28,220 --> 00:25:33,980
Kayı can't make the Turks autonomous all
by itself.

228
00:25:36,140 --> 00:25:38,740
This will bring the end of Kayıs.

229
00:25:43,860 --> 00:25:50,820
Thus, all Turks will lose their hope
eventually.

230
00:25:56,300 --> 00:26:00,940
Do you agree with your brother and uncle?

231
00:26:03,060 --> 00:26:08,300
Anything can be an illusion if we believe
so.

232
00:26:12,620 --> 00:26:17,940
Once we start our own path in the name of
Allah as well as faith and effort...

233
00:26:21,420 --> 00:26:23,700
... only then our dreams will come true.

234
00:26:29,300 --> 00:26:34,540
Even Çobanoğulları belive in this dream
and fight against Geyhatu by themselves.

235
00:26:35,220 --> 00:26:40,820
But, the most noble sons of Oğuz Kağan
are just watching them.

236
00:26:42,620 --> 00:26:43,740
Is this proper?

237
00:26:44,460 --> 00:26:45,820
Is this who we really are?

238
00:26:45,860 --> 00:26:46,780
Tell me!

239
00:26:59,980 --> 00:27:03,460
Let's say Çobanoğulları wants to meet
their death.

240
00:27:06,220 --> 00:27:08,660
Would you want your Tent to end up in the
same way?

241
00:27:10,860 --> 00:27:12,580
I'm the son of Ertuğrul Gazi.

242
00:27:15,360 --> 00:27:18,680
I don't put my Tent into
a war they will lose.

243
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:23,560
But...

244
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:30,320
If death is inevitable,
and the end of this battle is testimony...

245
00:27:31,080 --> 00:27:33,400
Then...

246
00:27:33,560 --> 00:27:40,520
I'll run into testimony with my valiants
who dedicated their lives for our cause!

247
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:54,880
My creator gave me one last
chance to see my Tents state...

248
00:27:54,880 --> 00:28:00,720
... and to declare my will.

249
00:28:06,320 --> 00:28:11,680
Put your differences aside
and unite!

250
00:28:20,280 --> 00:28:26,280
We need to take care of Nikola before
Geyhatu returns from tabriz.

251
00:28:29,640 --> 00:28:32,280
After that...

252
00:28:34,720 --> 00:28:42,040
... we'll choose a new Bey
everyone will unite under.

253
00:28:49,360 --> 00:28:55,000
A Bey shines out
in such harsh times.

254
00:28:59,880 --> 00:29:04,760
Your attitudes will determine
which one of you will be the Bey.

255
00:29:11,120 --> 00:29:18,000
All men will see the new Bey.

256
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:29,560
Know that those who are separated
will be left desperate!

257
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:45,880
Now. What shall we do
to take down that infidel Nikola?

258
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:47,960
Talk!

259
00:29:58,680 --> 00:30:03,640
That man came to life.
How does this happen, Lena?

260
00:30:06,040 --> 00:30:10,840
What if he announces the Bey?
What if he chooses Osman?

261
00:30:15,760 --> 00:30:23,440
Lena? What is it?
How are you this relaxed?

262
00:30:26,720 --> 00:30:33,960
Don’t you think about what will happen
if he chooses Osman instead of Savcı?

263
00:30:37,320 --> 00:30:41,400
It seems like you want Savcı to
be the Bey more than me, Hazal Hatun.

264
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:50,120
Thanks to Allah, Ertuğrul Bey
is back on his feet again.

265
00:30:56,280 --> 00:30:58,840
What are they up to this time?

266
00:31:04,920 --> 00:31:07,560
It’s hard to wait, isn’t it, Hatuns?

267
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:13,840
What is it, Selcan Hatun? You look
like you received some good news.

268
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:16,640
Did someone tell you something?

269
00:31:17,800 --> 00:31:23,880
Yes. Ertuğrul Bey
told me before anyone else.

270
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:32,520
While Osman and Savcı
are fighting over it…

271
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:36,240
… I’ll choose my brother
Dündar who thinks he’ll be the Bey.

272
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:43,280
I’ll add something to that.

273
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:46,600
Those who team up for their own benefits…

274
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:48,600
… separate swiftly.

275
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:55,120
What I’m saying is,
watch out for each other.

276
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:58,520
Or you’ll be separated soon, Allah forbid.

277
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:18,280
Patience…

278
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:25,080
Tell me, son.
Which path should the Kayıs follow?

279
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:28,320
We need to enter
the infidels’ den, my Bey.

280
00:32:29,920 --> 00:32:33,240
I say we gather all
the Alps and march to İnegöl.

281
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:41,600
What do you say, Dündar?

282
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:46,760
My Bey. Since
the snake’s head is in İnegöl…

283
00:32:46,760 --> 00:32:51,440
… we shall go there and cut it.

284
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:01,280
Let’s siege İnegöl first.

285
00:33:01,280 --> 00:33:06,360
Because if we kick Nikola out of there,
he won’t have a place to hold on to.

286
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:15,520
I think Osman is glad to hear that.

287
00:33:21,200 --> 00:33:23,480
I do not agree.

288
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:37,800
I say I don’t want any
disagreements and you oppose everyone.

289
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:43,760
Do we give up on
the truth if everyone opposes it?

290
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:51,960
What is that truth?
What is on your mind?

291
00:33:53,520 --> 00:33:58,160
If we siege İnegöl Fortress
now, we’ll lose too many men.

292
00:34:03,560 --> 00:34:10,400
We need to ambush
Nikola’s soldiers and weaken him.

293
00:34:16,080 --> 00:34:18,440
How will you accomplish that?

294
00:34:19,440 --> 00:34:22,440
Nikola thinks that
Targun Hatun is still his spy.

295
00:34:23,440 --> 00:34:25,560
He gets the news from her.

296
00:34:28,520 --> 00:34:32,800
He trusts her more since
he heard that she’ll marry me.

297
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:36,880
He’ll listen to every word she says.

298
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:39,600
My tricks are ready.

299
00:34:42,639 --> 00:34:45,840
Targun Hatun is probably
already on her way.

300
00:35:01,680 --> 00:35:03,600
What is that trick?

301
00:35:08,760 --> 00:35:14,280
What did you do, Cuman Girl?
Did you poison Kayı’s Beys?

302
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:17,240
Did you kill all of them?

303
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:20,520
They are all alive.

304
00:35:24,200 --> 00:35:28,080
What did I tell you?
Should I slit your throat right here?

305
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:31,200
What did I tell you?

306
00:35:33,120 --> 00:35:36,720
Tell me.
Come on.

307
00:35:38,160 --> 00:35:41,680
Savcı Bey is trying
to be the Bey by force.

308
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:45,520
Osman Bey stood in his way.

309
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:50,200
Ertuğrul Bey all of a sudden stood
up and gathered everyone in a meeting.

310
00:35:50,880 --> 00:35:53,920
When was I supposed
to poison them, Nikola?

311
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:59,960
How was I supposed to poison
those who always fight and never eat?

312
00:36:03,120 --> 00:36:08,280
Did Ertuğrul Bey stood up?

313
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:15,440
Yes. But he’s still in bad condition.
Everyone is with him in the Tent.

314
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:17,360
And I came here.

315
00:36:17,360 --> 00:36:22,000
Just as they were about to fight each
other, Ertuğrul Bey stood up. Is that it?

316
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:24,920
And now are they sitting and talking?

317
00:36:26,200 --> 00:36:31,040
Flatyos! Is that God
of your on the Turks’ side?

318
00:36:32,080 --> 00:36:36,000
God is with those who
follow the path of Jesus Christ.

319
00:36:41,920 --> 00:36:47,840
Do you have anything
useful to say, Cuman Girl?

320
00:36:52,680 --> 00:36:54,680
Yes, I do.

321
00:36:56,680 --> 00:37:00,120
I told Osman Bey that I won’t
be marrying him before saving my father.

322
00:37:01,520 --> 00:37:05,520
So, he’s now preparing to save my father.

323
00:37:14,600 --> 00:37:22,480
How is Osman going to
save your father? Will he attack İnegöl?

324
00:37:22,480 --> 00:37:25,400
How will he do that?

325
00:37:25,720 --> 00:37:29,200
I played the trick instead
of you this time, Nikola.

326
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:37,160
You. tricks. Did you?

327
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:43,080
What kind of a trick are
you playing, Cuman girl?

328
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:52,640
Targun Hatun will convince Nikola
to bring her father to Kurtboğazı[İnegöl].

329
00:37:53,720 --> 00:37:57,160
Are you sure Nikola
will take this bait, brother?

330
00:37:57,160 --> 00:38:01,520
He won’t, brother. But he won’t
care because I’ll be there.

331
00:38:03,560 --> 00:38:08,560
Instead of İnegöl’s walls,
we’ll battle Nikola’s men.

332
00:38:16,680 --> 00:38:23,720
This is how we defeat Nikola.

333
00:38:27,600 --> 00:38:34,200
Not a fortress battle,
but a battle of tricks.

334
00:38:40,800 --> 00:38:46,160
And an opportunity for you
to work together. What do you say?

335
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:56,840
Even if it looks dangerous
if that’s what our father wants…

336
00:38:58,800 --> 00:39:01,520
… that’s how it will move.

337
00:39:04,760 --> 00:39:11,160
Since the orders come from
our Bey, all we can do is to obey.

338
00:39:13,440 --> 00:39:20,560
Don’t worry, father.
We’ll do everything necessary.

339
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:34,520
Osman.
Start the preparations.

340
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:38,000
We start tomorrow.

341
00:39:49,040 --> 00:39:51,960
As you wish, my Bey.

342
00:40:05,040 --> 00:40:08,880
I’ll tell Osman Bey that you’ll
take my father to Kurtboğazı.

343
00:40:09,400 --> 00:40:11,800
What if he doesn’t believe you?

344
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:14,960
Looks like you don’t
know me yet, Flatyos.

345
00:40:15,480 --> 00:40:21,040
I’ll bring Osman Bey to
Kurtboğazı and you’ll bring my father.

346
00:40:21,040 --> 00:40:25,160
The rest is yours.
I’ll leave with my father…

347
00:40:25,160 --> 00:40:29,040
… and will never see
your evil faces again.

348
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:37,080
Not bad, Cuman girl.
Not bad at all.

349
00:40:38,080 --> 00:40:46,160
Targun Hatun. We’ll bring
your father to Kurtboğazı. And…

350
00:40:47,280 --> 00:40:52,800
… after one little
mistake, your father will die.

351
00:40:54,240 --> 00:41:00,080
So will you.

352
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:06,720
Now go. Don’t make
future husband worried.

353
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:26,440
What do you say, Flatyos?

354
00:41:27,040 --> 00:41:30,280
I think this is a trap, Nikola.

355
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:35,320
Maybe. But this is
still a really good opportunity.

356
00:41:36,520 --> 00:41:41,920
We’ll take precautions.
We’ll act like they are setting up a trap.

357
00:41:41,920 --> 00:41:46,520
Then, Flatyos, we’ll
win the war.

358
00:41:58,120 --> 00:42:01,880
First, Ertuğrul Bey
got up from his death bed.

359
00:42:01,880 --> 00:42:04,520
Then, this ambush thing.

360
00:42:08,360 --> 00:42:11,160
I worry about you.

361
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:24,080
At least my father
didn’t ask about yesterday.

362
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:29,640
Otherwise neither Osman
nor I would have got what we wanted.

363
00:42:30,760 --> 00:42:37,880
Out of the blue, we would
be the same as Gündüz and Dündar.

364
00:42:42,600 --> 00:42:50,040
You say out of the blue. But you don’t
think that this could be Dündar’s plan.

365
00:42:56,000 --> 00:43:03,920
You say that you won’t give up.
May Allah give you strength.

366
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:12,240
Uncle. Is our
agreement still valid?

367
00:43:12,240 --> 00:43:16,360
Sure it is, my nephew.

368
00:43:16,720 --> 00:43:19,760
This ambition makes brothers
fight each other, Lena.

369
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:26,120
Why would my Uncle stay away?
He also has a plan for sure.

370
00:43:31,840 --> 00:43:34,080
I have some good news for you.

371
00:43:35,120 --> 00:43:39,320
Bayhoca is on his way.
He’ll be in the Tent shortly.

372
00:43:42,760 --> 00:43:46,160
My dear son!
I missed him so much.

373
00:43:47,560 --> 00:43:49,880
I can’t wait to hug him!

374
00:43:49,880 --> 00:43:54,040
I also missed him a lot.

375
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:16,360
Everything will be as
we wish, my Savcı.

376
00:44:18,200 --> 00:44:23,040
Inshallah.

377
00:44:50,640 --> 00:44:52,480
Osman Bey…

378
00:44:53,800 --> 00:45:00,800
Everything started as a
trick, continued as a trick.

379
00:45:37,400 --> 00:45:40,520
Are you that Osman Bey
whom they are afraid of?

380
00:45:40,520 --> 00:45:45,680
I am. From now on,
you’re safe with us.

381
00:45:45,680 --> 00:45:48,640
I was in it to save my father.

382
00:45:51,200 --> 00:45:55,760
But I can’t even save myself now.

383
00:46:09,360 --> 00:46:12,320
I’m a prisoner
of your eyes.

384
00:46:12,320 --> 00:46:15,200
I fell prey to your strong arms.

385
00:46:18,560 --> 00:46:23,560
What will I do know?
I’m eating my heart out.

386
00:46:29,240 --> 00:46:32,800
Now you’re in
Bala’s arms, Osman Bey.

387
00:46:35,680 --> 00:46:38,280
And I’m in pain.

388
00:46:45,640 --> 00:46:47,280
Oh, Osman Bey…

389
00:47:19,240 --> 00:47:24,440
I can’t stand it.

390
00:47:56,960 --> 00:48:01,560
Look at you!

391
00:48:03,960 --> 00:48:06,560
Look at these beautiful eyes.

392
00:48:09,040 --> 00:48:12,560
One day, I’ll be held
responsible for these eyes.

393
00:48:16,840 --> 00:48:20,040
It’s been a while since
you talked about my eyes.

394
00:48:21,440 --> 00:48:24,040
My Bala…

395
00:48:25,240 --> 00:48:30,240
Since my father has
fallen ill, I can’t see anything.

396
00:48:30,960 --> 00:48:34,720
But now he’s up and ready for battle.

397
00:48:36,480 --> 00:48:40,000
I regenerated, my Bala.

398
00:48:43,320 --> 00:48:51,080
Is it just the eyes?
What about these hairs?

399
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:56,880
What about these hairs?

400
00:49:06,040 --> 00:49:14,160
A planet for each curl,
a city for each strand…

401
00:49:22,120 --> 00:49:24,200
My Osman…

402
00:49:25,520 --> 00:49:27,640
I pray for a child.

403
00:49:32,960 --> 00:49:37,080
I want it to be from me,
not from another Hatun.

404
00:49:38,960 --> 00:49:43,640
Me too, my Bala.
I also pray for it.

405
00:49:45,760 --> 00:49:48,360
I want you to give
me a successor.

406
00:49:49,240 --> 00:49:53,840
I want my children
to have your noble spirit.

407
00:49:57,040 --> 00:50:03,000
In them, I want to see a Kayı Bey’s
ambition for battle, and your clean heart.

408
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:09,520
My Bala…

409
00:50:12,280 --> 00:50:14,200
Let’s pray.

410
00:50:15,360 --> 00:50:19,920
Let’s call upon our Allah who
wants us to pray for everything.

411
00:50:23,560 --> 00:50:25,880
May I enter, my Bey?

412
00:50:34,000 --> 00:50:36,320
Targun Hatun?

413
00:50:38,520 --> 00:50:40,720
What is it, Targun Hatun?

414
00:51:17,120 --> 00:51:20,480
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
[In the name of Allah, the merciful, the compassionate]

415
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:23,640
My Allah...

416
00:51:26,560 --> 00:51:28,160
I'm coming to you.

417
00:51:29,360 --> 00:51:36,200
You invite me to reunite
and let go.

418
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:44,320
Accept me to your Heaven which
my Halime wanders around in.

419
00:51:45,120 --> 00:51:51,600
Make me reach my martyr brothers...
... my father Süleiman Şah...

420
00:51:54,960 --> 00:51:58,480
... my mother Hayme Hatun.

421
00:51:59,680 --> 00:52:03,960
Keep my Tent safe.

422
00:52:04,920 --> 00:52:09,240
Protect it.

423
00:52:27,920 --> 00:52:30,280
I came to say this...

424
00:52:31,400 --> 00:52:34,120
I...
Uhm...

425
00:52:41,640 --> 00:52:47,240
Thank you for what you
did for my father, Osman Bey.

426
00:52:53,560 --> 00:52:55,960
I can't forget
what you did for me.

427
00:52:57,440 --> 00:52:59,040
I came to say these.

428
00:52:59,840 --> 00:53:07,400
Targun Hatun. Thank me after
I save your father tomorrow.

429
00:53:08,320 --> 00:53:10,920
You're right, my Bey.

430
00:53:13,280 --> 00:53:17,200
It's a little eary.
Actually, it's a little late!

431
00:53:21,320 --> 00:53:23,240
I mean, I came at a late hour.

432
00:53:24,600 --> 00:53:26,240
I should leave.

433
00:53:29,720 --> 00:53:36,120
- Good night to you.
- Good night.

434
00:54:35,840 --> 00:54:40,480
My Kayı Tent...
My mighty Tent...

435
00:54:41,640 --> 00:54:46,680
Me ancestor Süleiman Şah...

436
00:54:47,040 --> 00:54:50,280
My mother Hayme mother...

437
00:54:50,280 --> 00:54:54,720
My Hatun...
My sweet Halime...

438
00:54:54,720 --> 00:54:59,560
My brother Gündoğdu...
my brother Sungurtekin...

439
00:55:00,080 --> 00:55:02,400
My brother Dündar...

440
00:55:02,400 --> 00:55:07,000
Second mother to my children,
Selcan Hatun...

441
00:55:07,000 --> 00:55:14,200
My brave Valiants...
Turgut, Bamsı, Abdurrahman, Doğan...

442
00:55:14,880 --> 00:55:20,560
My children...
Gündüz, Savcı, my Osman...

443
00:55:21,320 --> 00:55:23,480
My saint people...

444
00:55:24,720 --> 00:55:27,760
Give me your blessings.

445
00:55:30,640 --> 00:55:32,120
My creator...

446
00:55:35,000 --> 00:55:37,240
My father passed it down to me.

447
00:55:38,000 --> 00:55:46,000
Don't let my children and
grandchildren have this illness.

448
00:56:00,440 --> 00:56:04,440
He had Kayı on his mind.

449
00:56:05,480 --> 00:56:11,240
His children...
The battle we'll fight tomorrow.

450
00:56:13,480 --> 00:56:23,080
Abdurrahman Gazi. Tell me
Will we ever see such a Bey again?

451
00:56:24,040 --> 00:56:30,760
We won't, brother.
We won't see someone like my Bey.

452
00:56:33,680 --> 00:56:35,680
But brother...

453
00:56:38,480 --> 00:56:42,760
What is he doing inside?
He doesn't make any sound.

454
00:56:44,160 --> 00:56:48,440
- Did he?
- Brother...

455
00:56:58,800 --> 00:57:02,320
I'm fine.
Don't worry.

456
00:57:11,600 --> 00:57:20,440
After Osman ambushes Nikola tomorrow,
he'll have a trick ready for sure.

457
00:57:27,800 --> 00:57:31,800
He'll keep Flatyos as a backup.

458
00:57:32,760 --> 00:57:37,600
Don't worry, my Bey.
We'll take all necessary precautions.

459
00:57:42,440 --> 00:57:46,040
No. Listen.

460
00:57:48,720 --> 00:57:55,600
If Flatyos is waiting to ambush,
Savcı and Gündüz will flank him.

461
00:57:56,200 --> 00:58:00,840
Don't worry, my Bey.
Do your heart good.

462
00:58:02,840 --> 00:58:05,040
Keep your eyes open.

463
00:58:05,040 --> 00:58:08,880
- We will, my Bey.
- Thank you, my Bey.

464
00:58:24,040 --> 00:58:31,000
My Bey. You should rest.

465
00:58:40,320 --> 00:58:43,400
Come on. You should rest too.

466
00:58:45,080 --> 00:58:50,960
- As your order.
- As you order, my Bey.

467
00:59:34,800 --> 00:59:39,000
Bamsı.
Abdurrahman.

468
00:59:41,120 --> 00:59:43,760
May you live long, my Valiants.

469
01:00:43,720 --> 01:00:52,920
What have I done?
I can't stand it.

470
01:00:57,680 --> 01:01:00,640
I can't stand seeing him
with someone else.

471
01:01:03,360 --> 01:01:07,440
Bala...

472
01:01:08,840 --> 01:01:11,560
You can't give him a child.

473
01:01:13,840 --> 01:01:15,920
But I will!

474
01:01:17,560 --> 01:01:20,360
You will see!

475
01:01:21,480 --> 01:01:27,360
I will take him from you.
You'll see.

476
01:01:32,960 --> 01:01:34,440
It's not wrong.

477
01:01:39,720 --> 01:01:45,400
It's not wrong to love him.
Or want him.

478
01:01:49,440 --> 01:01:51,200
It's not wrong.

479
01:02:16,960 --> 01:02:19,960
Osman Bey!

480
01:02:21,120 --> 01:02:23,760
What is it, Abdurrahman Gazi?

481
01:02:24,320 --> 01:02:29,360
It's important. You've taken
your weapons for a battle.

482
01:02:30,320 --> 01:02:33,920
But Ertuğrul Bey
doesn't want you to go.

483
01:02:47,160 --> 01:02:51,560
What are you saying, Abdurrahman Gazi?
He doesn't want me to?

484
01:02:55,560 --> 01:02:59,000
My brothers are going to a battle
with the ambush I've set up.

485
01:03:00,160 --> 01:03:02,040
Do you want me to sit here?

486
01:03:02,480 --> 01:03:05,160
- My Osman...
- What will they do without me?

487
01:03:06,520 --> 01:03:10,400
As you know, I don't
question Ertuğrul Bey's orders.

488
01:03:12,960 --> 01:03:16,520
He told me to inform you.
And I did.

489
01:03:23,320 --> 01:03:27,280
What does he want me to do?
Did he tell you?

490
01:03:29,240 --> 01:03:31,240
My Osman...

491
01:03:33,680 --> 01:03:39,600
Ertuğrul Bey is waiting for you
at Halime Hatun's grave.

492
01:03:46,800 --> 01:03:51,320
- Thank you, Abdurrahman Gazi.
- Thank you.

493
01:04:15,910 --> 01:04:17,900
MashaAllah (praise be).

494
01:04:31,818 --> 01:04:36,608
We are all coming from soil.

495
01:04:42,877 --> 01:04:48,797
And the soil is going to end us.

496
01:04:49,384 --> 01:04:53,548
But I think it will take Osman sooner.

497
01:04:53,548 --> 01:04:56,358
What are you planning, Nicola?

498
01:04:56,463 --> 01:05:04,463
Sometimes you get bored of being yourself.
For example, I am going to be a Turk today.

499
01:05:06,118 --> 01:05:08,128
We are ready, Nicola.

500
01:05:20,601 --> 01:05:24,081
Is this governor Nicola?

501
01:05:31,634 --> 01:05:38,124
I think the only thing resembles to me is
my sculputre, which has to be done by me.

502
01:05:43,230 --> 01:05:49,100
Do not forget that you are representing me

503
01:05:49,762 --> 01:05:53,852
Why are you doing this?
What are you after, hah?

504
01:05:55,147 --> 01:05:59,957
İnal Bey, I am thrilled
and can't control it.

505
01:06:00,413 --> 01:06:04,473
Do you know who your daughter is going to
bring me to save you?

506
01:06:05,822 --> 01:06:09,074
- Osman.
- Not possible!

507
01:06:09,074 --> 01:06:11,564
My daughter wouldn't do that!

508
01:06:13,749 --> 01:06:20,119
She loves you. I hope she does it, İnal
Bey, I hope she does.

509
01:06:20,262 --> 01:06:26,402
- If not, both you and your daughter dies.
- You ignoble dog!

510
01:06:36,486 --> 01:06:40,456
I smell death, Vladius.

511
01:06:44,563 --> 01:06:47,183
Get in position.

512
01:07:50,277 --> 01:07:53,037
I'll take revenge for you today, father.

513
01:08:24,276 --> 01:08:29,146
- We are getting close to the battlefield.
- Big day, huh Savcı?

514
01:08:31,198 --> 01:08:35,034
We are going to make those dogs pay
if Allah permits, brother.

515
01:08:35,034 --> 01:08:38,464
Inshallah brother, Inshallah.

516
01:08:40,279 --> 01:08:43,139
We are going on foot from here.

517
01:08:44,243 --> 01:08:48,253
Alps, we are going to be silent
as death.

518
01:09:28,005 --> 01:09:31,725
My Halime.
The light of my heart.

519
01:09:33,858 --> 01:09:36,728
It's time.

520
01:09:38,783 --> 01:09:46,343
I yearn for you.
A gazelle took me to you.

521
01:09:46,383 --> 01:09:49,410
An angel took me to you.

522
01:09:49,452 --> 01:09:55,332
Now, that angel will recouple us.

523
01:10:03,287 --> 01:10:05,067
My angel.

524
01:10:05,808 --> 01:10:10,638
My happiness, my woman.

525
01:10:20,009 --> 01:10:24,979
We are going to walk together in
heaven.

526
01:10:25,469 --> 01:10:30,559
You and I will be together forever.

527
01:10:31,881 --> 01:10:35,211
All the pain is gone.

528
01:10:35,763 --> 01:10:39,943
Eternity is the gift for our patience.

529
01:10:41,549 --> 01:10:45,489
What a bliss to live with you.

530
01:10:47,178 --> 01:10:50,618
I'll come to you when I die.

531
01:11:08,415 --> 01:11:11,255
Look who is coming.

532
01:11:16,685 --> 01:11:19,145
Our Dark Osman.

533
01:11:22,341 --> 01:11:25,211
He is down at the mouth again.

534
01:11:26,923 --> 01:11:30,593
He reproaches to me.

535
01:11:33,491 --> 01:11:37,421
He asks me why I didn't let him fight.

536
01:12:11,878 --> 01:12:14,298
Salaimun Aleikum
(May peace be upon you)

537
01:12:14,981 --> 01:12:17,061
Alaikum Salam.
(And unto you peace)

538
01:13:20,338 --> 01:13:22,318
They are getting close, sir.

539
01:13:23,302 --> 01:13:29,645
Don't forget, we are going to kill them
before they got Nicola.

540
01:13:29,645 --> 01:13:31,295
Yes sir.

541
01:13:55,405 --> 01:13:57,035
They are coming.

542
01:14:09,205 --> 01:14:11,395
Let's do it.

543
01:14:12,412 --> 01:14:14,552
Our father was right, brother.

544
01:14:16,619 --> 01:14:20,849
They set a trap before we arrive in
Nicola's place.

545
01:14:29,978 --> 01:14:32,398
They are in the bush.

546
01:14:32,996 --> 01:14:35,940
May our holy war be blessed, brother.

547
01:14:35,940 --> 01:14:37,920
Etvallah (thank you)

548
01:15:12,643 --> 01:15:16,863
Here we are in their base.

549
01:15:23,596 --> 01:15:26,539
Infidel Nicola is also there.

550
01:15:26,539 --> 01:15:30,139
You become happy when you see the infidel,
Bamsı Bey.

551
01:15:34,164 --> 01:15:38,584
Bamsı Bey gets younger at the war time,
don't you know that, Göktuğ?

552
01:15:39,054 --> 01:15:43,464
Sons, we are going to attack suddenly.

553
01:16:03,452 --> 01:16:05,459
Ya Allah!

554
01:16:05,779 --> 01:16:08,349
Allah is eternal!

555
01:17:06,074 --> 01:17:11,284
İnal Bey, you Turks say war is full
of tricks.

556
01:17:11,640 --> 01:17:14,650
But you know what is the real trick?

557
01:17:14,698 --> 01:17:17,948
The trap in another trap.

558
01:17:19,369 --> 01:17:21,519
Yeah, yeah.

559
01:17:52,932 --> 01:17:55,202
Savcı Bey and Gündüz Bey.

560
01:18:27,454 --> 01:18:30,894
We are trapped!
Attack! Attack!

561
01:18:30,974 --> 01:18:34,294
- Allah is eternal!
- Allah is rightous!

562
01:18:49,090 --> 01:18:54,620
War never stops for a Ghazi, son.

563
01:18:56,955 --> 01:18:59,735
Nicole goes, someone else shows up.

564
01:19:00,965 --> 01:19:03,445
War never ends.

565
01:19:05,745 --> 01:19:10,475
However, Ertuğrul Ghazi is leaving.

566
01:19:15,936 --> 01:19:18,786
May Allah give you a long life., my Bey.

567
01:19:24,013 --> 01:19:29,483
This is our last private conversation.

568
01:19:36,145 --> 01:19:39,105
Yes it is, Osman.

569
01:19:41,666 --> 01:19:48,356
I love all three of you.
I don't discriminate you.

570
01:19:50,248 --> 01:19:52,858
Because you are my sons.

571
01:19:56,068 --> 01:20:01,468
But you have a special place.

572
01:20:04,798 --> 01:20:09,038
You are going to success huge events.

573
01:20:11,281 --> 01:20:14,311
You are going to get ahead of me.

574
01:20:15,184 --> 01:20:17,984
Nobody can get ahead of you.

575
01:20:18,176 --> 01:20:20,946
No one can, father.

576
01:20:22,510 --> 01:20:24,480
You will!

577
01:20:26,481 --> 01:20:30,861
If you can't get ahead of me, I won't
give my blessings to you1

578
01:20:34,353 --> 01:20:37,873
You have been carrying Kayı Beys
like a lion...

579
01:20:38,349 --> 01:20:43,589
since I started the war.

580
01:20:45,655 --> 01:20:50,365
As long as that lion carries us...

581
01:20:50,808 --> 01:20:53,098
we are going to destroy whoever we
encounter...

582
01:20:54,330 --> 01:20:59,050
and make Turks the victorious ones!

583
01:21:00,611 --> 01:21:05,051
But if you try to let that lion go...

584
01:21:06,742 --> 01:21:09,252
he is going to kill all of us.

585
01:21:09,770 --> 01:21:14,340
The war will never stop.

586
01:21:16,047 --> 01:21:20,297
It will be greater, and it should be.

587
01:21:24,242 --> 01:21:29,843
- This is my objective, my father.
- Here in front of your mother's grave...

588
01:21:29,843 --> 01:21:32,023
you need to promise me.

589
01:21:35,932 --> 01:21:41,172
I promise you, father.
I will protect our tradition.

590
01:21:42,637 --> 01:21:45,297
I will secure the justice.

591
01:21:46,112 --> 01:21:51,482
I will be compassionate to my people.
I will listen to them.

592
01:21:53,365 --> 01:21:59,985
Kayıs state is going to be home for the
oppressed...

593
01:22:00,414 --> 01:22:05,964
it is going to be a shelter for all the
Turks.

594
01:22:10,472 --> 01:22:12,802
I promise you father.

595
01:22:16,035 --> 01:22:21,175
Long live.
May Allah give you victories.

596
01:22:22,284 --> 01:22:27,714
May your name carry on!

597
01:22:47,585 --> 01:22:50,595
- My Father.
- Son.

598
01:22:52,289 --> 01:22:54,609
My valiant father!

599
01:23:36,082 --> 01:23:38,122
Father!

600
01:23:41,846 --> 01:23:44,476
Father! Father!

601
01:23:44,478 --> 01:23:46,298
I'll save you father.

602
01:23:47,160 --> 01:23:49,790
You traitor!

603
01:24:08,478 --> 01:24:10,908
Targun Hatun, trap!

604
01:24:28,100 --> 01:24:33,110
Bamsı Bey, this is injustice!
two versus one.

605
01:24:35,772 --> 01:24:37,902
You are crazy.

606
01:24:40,438 --> 01:24:43,388
You are crazy, good.

607
01:24:44,740 --> 01:24:48,760
Crazy governor.
You know what they say.

608
01:24:49,135 --> 01:24:52,695
Crazy finds crazy.
Come here!

609
01:25:36,850 --> 01:25:39,810
Damn it! Attack!

610
01:25:45,859 --> 01:25:49,119
You are mine today, dog!

611
01:25:50,577 --> 01:25:55,187
You are going to die today, Savcı!

612
01:26:39,752 --> 01:26:41,872
Damn you!

613
01:26:47,129 --> 01:26:51,239
I'll kill all of you!

614
01:27:54,481 --> 01:27:56,641
I'm your end, dog!

615
01:28:30,333 --> 01:28:34,143
We need him, brother, we need him.

616
01:28:39,889 --> 01:28:42,179
I'm not done with him yet.

617
01:29:59,802 --> 01:30:04,492
I promise you father.
I'll perform my mission.

618
01:30:04,590 --> 01:30:07,350
I'll secure the injustice.

619
01:30:09,599 --> 01:30:14,179
I promised to the Kayı.

620
01:30:15,768 --> 01:30:22,108
I promised to Kayı Bey in front of the
grave of Kayı Hatun.

621
01:30:25,014 --> 01:30:30,824
From now on, I can't break my promise.

622
01:30:33,028 --> 01:30:38,358
This is a huge promise.

623
01:30:39,596 --> 01:30:42,176
This is a heavy promise.

624
01:30:42,891 --> 01:30:47,971
Heey, Karayel, who carries me
from place to place.

625
01:30:48,792 --> 01:30:53,332
If I can't keep my promise...

626
01:30:53,963 --> 01:30:58,783
Then I will only be a unnecessary load
for you.

627
01:30:58,868 --> 01:31:04,258
Hey Karayel!
If I can't keep my promise...

628
01:31:05,007 --> 01:31:08,027
don't carry me!

629
01:31:08,670 --> 01:31:11,450
Don't be my friend!

630
01:31:11,521 --> 01:31:15,771
Trample me under your iron horshoes!

631
01:31:20,696 --> 01:31:22,956
I swear!

632
01:31:24,691 --> 01:31:29,711
I swear!
Let the world hear me!

633
01:31:58,150 --> 01:32:01,490
Thanks to Allah, Ertuğrul Bey.

634
01:32:01,939 --> 01:32:05,749
We get to see you again.

635
01:32:05,771 --> 01:32:12,461
I needed to see you before I return
to dust.

636
01:32:13,899 --> 01:32:16,919
So, the time has come.

637
01:32:19,925 --> 01:32:24,395
Kayı Bey is taking a new voyage.

638
01:32:26,595 --> 01:32:30,935
You are going to walk without
me from now on.

639
01:32:32,162 --> 01:32:38,442
The passenger's will enlightens the way,
Ertuğrul Bey.

640
01:32:40,390 --> 01:32:45,470
Who is going to enlighten our way
after you?

641
01:32:46,773 --> 01:32:51,383
Who is going to take over your sword?

642
01:32:51,402 --> 01:32:55,322
Who is going to take over your
noble aim?

643
01:32:57,324 --> 01:33:02,834
You'll have hard times ahead.

644
01:33:03,823 --> 01:33:08,573
You are going to need tough men
in times like this.

645
01:33:10,044 --> 01:33:14,434
The circle tightens.

646
01:33:14,436 --> 01:33:19,555
In order for this circle to break, you
are going to need a man...

647
01:33:19,555 --> 01:33:27,545
who is ready for clashes, whose aim
is only to be victorious...

648
01:33:28,023 --> 01:33:31,003
who can do anything for the
future of his community.

649
01:33:32,512 --> 01:33:38,112
Who has the gift, the intelligence?

650
01:33:40,105 --> 01:33:47,135
Who is going to do politics for
the new Turkish state?

651
01:33:47,735 --> 01:33:54,475
Who is going to create a new market
for the merchants of this country?

652
01:33:55,453 --> 01:34:00,623
Who is going to lead Ahis?

653
01:34:02,435 --> 01:34:10,305
Bey, he is the one to clear the way
to the horizon...

654
01:34:10,305 --> 01:34:13,355
he is the one who goes in front...

655
01:34:14,277 --> 01:34:17,347
he is the one who will pave the
way for Kayı.

656
01:34:20,204 --> 01:34:23,034
He is my son, Osman.

657
01:34:25,031 --> 01:34:30,771
He will conquer, he will rule in justice!

658
01:34:31,995 --> 01:34:35,705
He will show you the way.

659
01:34:37,141 --> 01:34:44,711
He is going to create a new state.

660
01:34:46,238 --> 01:34:50,788
May Allah praise your decision.

661
01:34:53,715 --> 01:34:59,665
We believe in Osman and his dawah.

662
01:35:00,999 --> 01:35:05,899
Osman is going to found the state
Turks have been waiting for.

663
01:35:07,985 --> 01:35:13,445
Our children are going to call that
state by his name!

664
01:35:15,947 --> 01:35:21,277
This voyage that goes
From Aleppo to Sögüt...

665
01:35:22,152 --> 01:35:28,922
is going to spread on Bursa, then İcle...

666
01:35:29,443 --> 01:35:34,163
and then to the other side!

667
01:35:34,939 --> 01:35:40,309
He put his hand on mine one night.

668
01:35:43,129 --> 01:35:47,639
He talked about the other side, hoping
that I could hear.

669
01:35:49,810 --> 01:35:57,260
He told me to carry on my name
to overseas.

670
01:36:00,625 --> 01:36:03,475
I realized that he is the heir.

671
01:36:04,932 --> 01:36:08,932
He was the only one among
my children who talked about seas...

672
01:36:11,901 --> 01:36:16,621
...who was able to take
the boundaries of the Kayı...

673
01:36:17,529 --> 01:36:19,849
...to offshores.

674
01:36:20,091 --> 01:36:26,781
Ertuğrul Bey, we are as great as
our dreams and efforts.

675
01:36:27,979 --> 01:36:31,979
Hail the Kayıs who make the Turks
dream of a state...

676
01:36:32,813 --> 01:36:38,843
...in these difficult times.

677
01:36:39,003 --> 01:36:44,263
Hail the ones who await...

678
01:36:44,684 --> 01:36:50,824
...who point the far afield
in these difficult times...

679
01:36:52,048 --> 01:37:00,318
...the infinite and holy state
that all Turks pay homage to.

680
01:37:19,671 --> 01:37:21,951
Ertuğrul Bey!

681
01:37:22,867 --> 01:37:25,807
Where is the target of the campaign?

682
01:37:35,301 --> 01:37:38,451
To Allah, who is the owner
of the realms.

683
01:38:05,587 --> 01:38:09,587
The secret is revealed!

684
01:38:15,414 --> 01:38:19,414
The secret is revealed!

685
01:38:59,101 --> 01:39:03,101
O' Osman son of Ertuğrul Ghazi!

686
01:39:03,700 --> 01:39:07,700
Are you ready?
O' son of the Bey!

687
01:39:07,700 --> 01:39:11,700
Are you ready for the great jihad?

688
01:39:12,597 --> 01:39:16,597
O' the one who speaks the
truth in the name of Allah...

689
01:39:17,461 --> 01:39:19,951
...tell me.

690
01:39:24,428 --> 01:39:31,108
Our prophet told the ones who returned
from jihad...

691
01:39:31,164 --> 01:39:36,754
...''Hail the ones who finished the little jihad,
the ones who'll have the great jihad forever''

692
01:39:43,573 --> 01:39:45,653
Osman Bey...

693
01:39:46,353 --> 01:39:51,703
...you know the little jihad.
Do you know the great jihad?

694
01:39:55,702 --> 01:40:02,552
Isn't great jihad the jihad against
our own desires?

695
01:40:03,086 --> 01:40:07,086
It is, son of the bey.
It is.

696
01:40:07,257 --> 01:40:11,257
But who is powerful enough
for this jihad?

697
01:40:15,427 --> 01:40:20,767
They don't discriminate among the
creatures that Allah created...

698
01:40:20,998 --> 01:40:26,018
...they don't make decisions before
seeing through things...

699
01:40:26,141 --> 01:40:31,071
...they don't call themselves victorious
before beating their desires.

700
01:40:34,335 --> 01:40:38,875
O' the one who speaks the truth
in the name of Allah!

701
01:40:42,011 --> 01:40:49,921
Tell me, is a son of a bey strong
enough for this jihad?

702
01:40:55,279 --> 01:41:01,259
Allah offered the escrow to mountains...

703
01:41:01,631 --> 01:41:05,041
...they didn't accept.

704
01:41:06,266 --> 01:41:10,266
Humans are cruel and ignorant.
They accepted it.

705
01:41:13,799 --> 01:41:21,129
Now it's our responsibility to carry
it and remember that it's an escrow.

706
01:41:24,440 --> 01:41:30,070
Don't think it's yours.
Don't think it's yours.

707
01:41:31,222 --> 01:41:37,012
In this world that you are a guest,
don't say that you are an owner.

708
01:41:41,786 --> 01:41:45,196
This is your jihad.

709
01:41:49,841 --> 01:41:54,901
The only owner is Allah, forever.

710
01:42:00,722 --> 01:42:04,722
Even if I lose this idea
for a day...

711
01:42:05,128 --> 01:42:10,468
...come again and remind me again.

712
01:42:14,955 --> 01:42:18,085
This is our job.

713
01:42:22,582 --> 01:42:25,162
Godspeed.

714
01:43:04,126 --> 01:43:09,696
He will choose one of his sons.
He didn't even consider me.

715
01:43:09,696 --> 01:43:15,756
In front of all the beys, he'll either
say Osman's or Savcı's name.

716
01:43:17,137 --> 01:43:21,137
The name that Ertuğrul Ghazi will
say...

717
01:43:21,137 --> 01:43:25,797
...will be an order for all the beys.

718
01:43:27,570 --> 01:43:32,310
You made your plans
based on Ertuğrul Bey's death...

719
01:43:32,310 --> 01:43:36,000
...but he resurrected.

720
01:43:36,000 --> 01:43:40,000
To ruin everything, he resurrected.

721
01:43:40,207 --> 01:43:42,307
Dündar Bey...

722
01:43:44,659 --> 01:43:48,659
Dündar, you should do something.

723
01:43:50,097 --> 01:43:55,217
Ertuğrul must die before...

724
01:43:55,420 --> 01:43:58,170
...saying that name.

725
01:44:03,449 --> 01:44:06,389
What are you saying, woman?

726
01:44:11,595 --> 01:44:17,705
Neither Ertuğrul, Savcı nor Osman
are of my concern!

727
01:44:18,605 --> 01:44:22,605
If you aren't going to
be the bey...

728
01:44:23,378 --> 01:44:29,308
...neither your tents nor your
future is of my concern!

729
01:44:31,412 --> 01:44:39,402
Because if you can't be the bey,
neither Savcı nor Osman will let us live.

730
01:44:40,605 --> 01:44:43,875
Understand that!

731
01:44:48,001 --> 01:44:55,271
They tried to hide behind the bushes.
They think they know the woods better we do.

732
01:44:57,908 --> 01:45:04,208
Mashallah, mashallah to my valiants.
We have beaten the heathens.

733
01:45:05,327 --> 01:45:09,957
It would be good to hit Nikola
like we hit Flatyos.

734
01:45:10,197 --> 01:45:14,517
His time will come,
his time will come.

735
01:45:15,431 --> 01:45:20,211
Our brother took his castle and
we ripped his right hand.

736
01:45:23,109 --> 01:45:25,339
I would've liked to come.

737
01:45:28,725 --> 01:45:32,405
I would want to chain Nikola.

738
01:45:33,103 --> 01:45:40,043
-But...
-But my father had to talk to you.

739
01:45:41,160 --> 01:45:46,250
Yes, brother.
We visited my mother's grave.

740
01:45:46,634 --> 01:45:51,724
-May Allah bless her.
-May Allah bless her.

741
01:45:52,699 --> 01:45:56,009
What were you doing there?

742
01:45:56,581 --> 01:46:00,581
-He wanted me to give a promise.
-What is that promise?

743
01:46:05,987 --> 01:46:09,567
He told me to protect the tents.

744
01:46:16,849 --> 01:46:22,799
Don't worry, both of you.
The tents are in safe hands.

745
01:46:27,618 --> 01:46:33,418
It is, it is. It is.
It is in safe hands.

746
01:46:34,822 --> 01:46:38,822
But now leave these aside.

747
01:46:43,684 --> 01:46:47,684
Ertuğrul Bey is gathering a great meeting.

748
01:46:48,814 --> 01:46:52,814
All the beys are invited.

749
01:46:55,299 --> 01:46:59,689
You should be ready too.

750
01:47:01,116 --> 01:47:02,406
Come on.

751
01:47:06,856 --> 01:47:09,006
Brothers.

752
01:47:10,732 --> 01:47:12,862
Maybe...

753
01:47:15,342 --> 01:47:18,232
...this is the last meeting
of our father.

754
01:47:29,602 --> 01:47:34,682
Beware, don't do something
that will upset him.

755
01:47:42,837 --> 01:47:48,877
This is a day of victory,
We should go to my father victorious.

756
01:47:51,188 --> 01:47:55,188
We'll, brother.
We'll.

757
01:48:07,840 --> 01:48:11,170
Mashallah. Mashallah.

758
01:48:25,299 --> 01:48:31,009
He lost too much blood. Go to the castle
and let them know that Nikola is well.

759
01:48:31,738 --> 01:48:34,548
Alps are searching everywhere for him.

760
01:48:38,430 --> 01:48:42,150
We can't allow that.
Go now.

761
01:48:57,698 --> 01:49:00,578
Nikola, it's me...

762
01:49:02,302 --> 01:49:06,152
Nikola, Nikola...

763
01:49:09,754 --> 01:49:12,484
Nikola you were killing me.

764
01:49:12,793 --> 01:49:16,793
I saved you from the alps
and brought you here.

765
01:49:22,981 --> 01:49:29,151
-You lost too much blood.
-I need to go to the castle.

766
01:49:29,151 --> 01:49:33,151
-No, no, no!
-I must go to the castle!

767
01:49:33,151 --> 01:49:37,911
Rome doesn't...
Rome doesn't lose!

768
01:49:37,911 --> 01:49:41,911
You lost too much blood.
You can't go.

769
01:49:42,892 --> 01:49:48,022
You are the last hope of our empire.

770
01:50:12,367 --> 01:50:18,337
-The castle, don't go to the castle.
-All right, Nikola.

771
01:50:32,068 --> 01:50:36,068
All right, all right, all right.

772
01:50:38,907 --> 01:50:40,997
Hang on.

773
01:50:41,911 --> 01:50:46,331
We can't lose...

774
01:50:48,415 --> 01:50:55,105
I don't lose, Rome doesn't lose...

775
01:50:55,599 --> 01:51:01,319
Rome doesn't lose, Rome can't lose...

776
01:51:21,367 --> 01:51:23,877
Flatyos...

777
01:51:30,572 --> 01:51:34,572
Flatyos the lion hunter.

778
01:51:34,594 --> 01:51:39,334
I wish they had left you to me.

779
01:51:40,377 --> 01:51:44,377
I wish they had left you over
to me.

780
01:51:44,381 --> 01:51:52,731
I would make you pay for the things you
did. The things you had done to Ayaz!

781
01:51:56,300 --> 01:52:01,710
Untie me and see me making
you regret your words, Göktuğ.

782
01:52:03,090 --> 01:52:07,090
Göktuğ Alp! Wait.

783
01:52:07,090 --> 01:52:11,090
I have more quarrel with the heathen.

784
01:52:13,180 --> 01:52:16,420
Open it.

785
01:52:38,798 --> 01:52:41,288
Savcı.

786
01:52:42,863 --> 01:52:48,963
Your father killed my father.
I will avenge him.

787
01:52:50,443 --> 01:52:53,563
Sooner or later.

788
01:53:06,235 --> 01:53:10,235
The day that I take your wife...

789
01:53:10,235 --> 01:53:13,065
...my Lena...

790
01:53:13,455 --> 01:53:17,455
...that day will be my revenge.

791
01:53:22,075 --> 01:53:25,275
You won't speak of my wife's name.

792
01:53:32,911 --> 01:53:39,271
This is what will I do to Nikola who holds
your leashes. I'll hang him.

793
01:54:02,773 --> 01:54:05,783
Göktuğ Alp!

794
01:54:10,031 --> 01:54:16,441
Watch this dog carefully.
He shouldn't die. He'll be hung.

795
01:54:33,920 --> 01:54:36,950
With the name of Allah.

796
01:54:37,729 --> 01:54:44,089
Allah who creates,
who puts faith into our hearts...

797
01:54:44,915 --> 01:54:48,915
...with Allah's ninety-nine names...

798
01:54:59,457 --> 01:55:03,457
My children, I congratulate your victory.

799
01:55:07,981 --> 01:55:14,791
May Allah destine you and our
tents with many victories.

800
01:55:14,791 --> 01:55:17,001
Amin! Amin!
Amin! Amin!

801
01:55:20,558 --> 01:55:27,468
These lands are conquered with the
blood and effort of the ghazis.

802
01:55:29,593 --> 01:55:33,903
The ones who jihaded in
the name of Allah...

803
01:55:33,903 --> 01:55:37,908
...gained the blessing of Allah.

804
01:55:39,716 --> 01:55:45,536
The ones left from
those Ghazis are...

805
01:55:49,014 --> 01:55:52,674
...Bamsı Bey and
Abdurrahman Ghazi.

806
01:55:56,005 --> 01:56:02,095
They are my will for you.

807
01:56:05,226 --> 01:56:10,896
Respect them as you respect me.

808
01:56:20,821 --> 01:56:25,181
My children, my beys...

809
01:56:25,325 --> 01:56:29,745
...I, Ertuğrul Ghazi son of Süleyman Shah.

810
01:56:30,257 --> 01:56:35,567
I'm about to hand over my escrow
that is my life.

811
01:56:40,245 --> 01:56:45,235
These are my last words
and...

812
01:56:46,872 --> 01:56:50,522
...my last advices.

813
01:56:53,765 --> 01:56:58,715
Open your ears and listen to me well.

814
01:57:05,809 --> 01:57:11,919
A state is the will of the people
that creates it...

815
01:57:13,550 --> 01:57:17,550
...and their...

816
01:57:18,702 --> 01:57:21,372
...consent.

817
01:57:24,322 --> 01:57:28,322
It's a place that protects...

818
01:57:28,867 --> 01:57:35,507
...the dignity and freedom
of the people.

819
01:57:37,775 --> 01:57:45,815
And for a Turk, the state is one more
thing than those things...

820
01:57:48,503 --> 01:57:54,043
It's an idea. That idea is protecting
all the oppressed...

821
01:57:54,043 --> 01:57:58,043
...regardless of their languages
or their religions...

822
01:57:58,043 --> 01:58:01,683
...against all the tyrants...

823
01:58:05,355 --> 01:58:10,695
...ruling with justice and
making the laws live.

824
01:58:12,311 --> 01:58:16,311
The eyes of the oppressed are on us...

825
01:58:16,613 --> 01:58:20,063
...their prayers are with you.

826
01:58:21,433 --> 01:58:25,433
If you bow down to slavery...

827
01:58:26,781 --> 01:58:32,631
...and see a tyrant state as legitimite,
whether it's Rum or Mongol...

828
01:58:34,011 --> 01:58:38,571
...how can the prayers of the oppressed
be true?

829
01:58:41,381 --> 01:58:45,931
How can justice be served?

830
01:58:49,171 --> 01:58:53,581
How can the laws live on?

831
01:59:01,407 --> 01:59:08,537
Whatever the price is, break the
chains of slavery.

832
01:59:14,321 --> 01:59:20,611
The flag of Kayıs can't bow down...

833
01:59:21,178 --> 01:59:27,528
...to any power except Allah's.

834
01:59:37,336 --> 01:59:41,336
Wherever the heathens gather...

835
01:59:41,794 --> 01:59:44,484
...an army...

836
01:59:48,514 --> 01:59:52,514
...the flag of Kayı...

837
01:59:52,663 --> 01:59:56,663
...and it's the noble Alps should stand.

838
02:00:04,426 --> 02:00:09,926
Those who don't believe in Allah's
victory...

839
02:00:09,996 --> 02:00:12,866
...deny the truth.

840
02:00:17,769 --> 02:00:23,039
First, be good muslims.

841
02:00:23,854 --> 02:00:29,564
Then, get ready for jihad.

842
02:00:31,919 --> 02:00:35,919
You'll see...

843
02:00:37,035 --> 02:00:40,705
...the victory will be yours.

844
02:00:52,301 --> 02:00:55,801
What you do is also jihad.

845
02:01:05,664 --> 02:01:11,384
If artisans and merchants
don't work right...

846
02:01:12,752 --> 02:01:17,932
...if they don't produce with
the sense of jihad...

847
02:01:19,463 --> 02:01:23,463
...the efforts of the Ghazis
will go in vain.

848
02:01:25,672 --> 02:01:28,642
The state can't grow.

849
02:01:29,851 --> 02:01:33,851
Every morning when
you get to work...

850
02:01:34,424 --> 02:01:38,424
...say that you are in jihad then.

851
02:01:40,355 --> 02:01:46,685
So, be like Davud Bey.

852
02:01:53,390 --> 02:01:56,670
Thank you, my bey.

853
02:02:29,805 --> 02:02:34,685
O' Kayıs...

854
02:02:34,685 --> 02:02:40,243
...do you think that I did my job right?

855
02:02:40,243 --> 02:02:42,753
We do, my bey.

856
02:02:45,870 --> 02:02:49,870
O' Kayıs...

857
02:02:53,382 --> 02:02:55,242
...do you give
me your blessings?

858
02:02:55,242 --> 02:02:57,422
We do, my bey!

859
02:03:02,920 --> 02:03:07,480
Now, if I announce
my heir to you...

860
02:03:12,976 --> 02:03:17,941
Will you respect him like you
respect me...

861
02:03:17,941 --> 02:03:22,741
...and follow all his orders?

862
02:03:22,741 --> 02:03:25,461
-We'll, my bey!
-We'll, my bey!

863
02:03:25,461 --> 02:03:28,421
We'll, my bey!
-We'll, my bey!

864
02:03:47,243 --> 02:03:54,313
My heir is...
I declare with peace in my heart...

865
02:03:55,715 --> 02:04:00,775
...that he will take my place...

866
02:04:00,775 --> 02:04:03,705
...the new Bey of Kayı...

867
02:04:09,432 --> 02:04:14,142
...is the one who never lets the
fire of jihad extinguish...

868
02:04:14,142 --> 02:04:19,048
...who carries the flag of Kayı
from one victory to another...

869
02:04:20,504 --> 02:04:26,274
...who doesn't accept slavery
or any chain...

870
02:04:31,963 --> 02:04:34,693
...my son...

871
02:05:13,922 --> 02:05:17,922
-My bey!
-Father! Father!

872
02:05:19,382 --> 02:05:23,382
Father!
Father!

873
02:05:26,419 --> 02:05:29,409
Father! Father!

874
02:05:32,918 --> 02:05:36,038
-Father!
-My bey...

875
02:05:42,918 --> 02:05:47,658
I bear witness that there is no god
but Allah...

876
02:05:49,867 --> 02:05:53,617
...and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the servant and Messenger of Allah

877
02:06:01,943 --> 02:06:05,123
Father! Father!

878
02:06:07,400 --> 02:06:09,630
Father!

879
02:06:11,144 --> 02:06:15,124
-Father!
-Father...

880
02:06:19,964 --> 02:06:22,104
My bey...

881
02:06:22,725 --> 02:06:25,135
Wait, father!

882
02:06:25,648 --> 02:06:27,788
Father!

883
02:06:34,199 --> 02:06:38,199
My bey is gone,
he is gone...

884
02:06:38,199 --> 02:06:41,249
He is gone!

885
02:06:43,247 --> 02:06:44,707
My bey...

886
02:06:54,014 --> 02:06:56,474
Bamsı Bey...

887
02:07:05,796 --> 02:07:09,056
-Brother...
-Father!

888
02:07:09,436 --> 02:07:13,026
My valiant father!

889
02:07:17,815 --> 02:07:20,825
My dear father...

890
02:07:22,635 --> 02:07:26,185
My Ghazi father...

891
02:07:52,490 --> 02:07:54,150
-Brother...

892
02:07:57,040 --> 02:08:00,184
No, no, no!

893
02:08:00,184 --> 02:08:00,750
No, no! No!
No, no, no!

894
02:08:00,750 --> 02:08:03,434
No, no! No!

895
02:08:03,566 --> 02:08:05,356
Brother!

896
02:08:08,046 --> 02:08:09,286
Gündüz Bey!

897
02:08:13,431 --> 02:08:14,821
Gündüz Bey.

898
02:08:16,905 --> 02:08:18,405
Brother...

899
02:08:25,559 --> 02:08:26,309
Father...

900
02:08:27,586 --> 02:08:28,846
My father...

901
02:08:56,134 --> 02:08:57,614
Bamsı Bey...

902
02:09:32,100 --> 02:09:33,320
Brothers...

903
02:09:38,026 --> 02:09:39,906
Our father is dead.

904
02:09:42,134 --> 02:09:43,584
Our father is dead...

905
02:09:46,040 --> 02:09:47,510
Our father is dead.

906
02:09:50,913 --> 02:09:52,543
Brother...

907
02:09:53,440 --> 02:09:54,800
Brother...

908
02:09:58,344 --> 02:09:59,574
From now on...

909
02:10:02,405 --> 02:10:05,025
we have a brother.

910
02:10:14,012 --> 02:10:15,902
I'd die for you.

911
02:10:16,183 --> 02:10:18,323
I'd die for you.

912
02:10:33,596 --> 02:10:37,316
My Bey is gone.

913
02:10:47,472 --> 02:10:49,102
I'd die for you.

914
02:11:04,106 --> 02:11:14,694
"Peace and prayer be upon You...

915
02:11:16,742 --> 02:11:26,062
O Messenger of Allah...

916
02:11:28,162 --> 02:11:38,482
peace and prayer be upon You...

917
02:11:38,892 --> 02:11:49,072
O loved by Allah...

918
02:11:49,661 --> 02:11:59,571
peace and prayer be upon You...

919
02:11:59,949 --> 02:12:09,389
O Prophet of Allah...

920
02:12:09,619 --> 02:12:18,769
peace and prayer be upon You...

921
02:12:18,917 --> 02:12:28,687
"O the Leader of past and future."

922
02:12:29,276 --> 02:12:35,726
"Your Allah, the Almighty and the Glorious,
has the glory above all of the men."

923
02:12:36,036 --> 02:12:39,773
"Peace be upon You, O Prophets...

924
02:12:39,883 --> 02:12:47,503
Praises are only to Allah, the Lord,
creator, teacher and tamer of the realms."
[Surah Az-Zumar - 39:1]

925
02:12:52,288 --> 02:12:54,508
Our Bey died!

926
02:12:55,907 --> 02:12:57,837
Our Bey died!

927
02:12:59,763 --> 02:13:01,963
Our Bey died!

928
02:13:05,800 --> 02:13:07,470
Our Bey died!

929
02:13:14,775 --> 02:13:17,705
- Our Ertuğrul Bey died!
- What are you saying, son?

930
02:13:19,581 --> 02:13:22,441
Our Ertuğrul Bey died!

931
02:13:33,185 --> 02:13:36,115
Our Ertuğrul Bey died!

932
02:14:00,178 --> 02:14:01,818
Died?

933
02:14:05,654 --> 02:14:07,664
He's dead.

934
02:14:25,519 --> 02:14:27,909
I couldn't take your revenge, father.

935
02:14:28,992 --> 02:14:31,822
Ertuğrul died himself.

936
02:14:35,429 --> 02:14:39,989
Forgive me. I promise you...

937
02:14:43,279 --> 02:14:45,619
I'll cause his family to die.

938
02:14:46,440 --> 02:14:51,080
I'll kill everyone who is his blood and
lay their bodies together.

939
02:14:52,957 --> 02:14:54,847
I promise.

940
02:15:00,105 --> 02:15:11,065
"Bismillah-ir-Rahman-ir-Rahim. (in the
name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate)

941
02:15:11,991 --> 02:15:15,801
Yâ-Sĩn.

942
02:15:16,110 --> 02:15:20,010
By the Quran, rich in wisdom!

943
02:15:20,433 --> 02:15:25,703
You ˹O Prophet˺ are truly
one of the messengers...

944
02:15:25,854 --> 02:15:31,304
upon the Straight Path.

945
02:15:31,935 --> 02:15:38,525
This is a revelation from the
Almighty, Most Merciful...

946
02:15:38,783 --> 02:15:44,113
so that you may warn a people...

947
02:15:44,113 --> 02:15:51,163
whose forefathers were
not warned, and so are heedless.

948
02:15:51,883 --> 02:15:57,743
The decree ˹of torment˺ has
already been justified...

949
02:15:57,743 --> 02:16:02,513
against most of them, for they will
never believe.

950
02:16:02,807 --> 02:16:06,807
˹It is as if˺ We have put shackles...

951
02:16:06,807 --> 02:16:10,807
around their necks up to their chins...

952
02:16:10,807 --> 02:16:17,087
so their heads are forced up,

953
02:16:18,433 --> 02:16:22,933
and have placed a barrier before them...

954
02:16:23,040 --> 02:16:27,390
and a barrier behind them...

955
02:16:27,713 --> 02:16:31,713
and covered them ˹all˺ up, so they fail
to see ˹the truth˺."

956
02:16:32,478 --> 02:16:36,478
"Verily we belong to Allah, and verily to
Him do we return."

957
02:16:36,983 --> 02:16:41,623
My Allah, accept the big
Ghazi to your heaven.

958
02:17:02,897 --> 02:17:07,997
"So glory be to the One in Whose Hands
is the authority over all things...

959
02:17:07,997 --> 02:17:15,427
and to Whom ˹alone˺ you will
˹all˺ be returned."

960
02:17:16,095 --> 02:17:19,815
"Allah Almighty speaks the truth.”

961
02:17:20,332 --> 02:17:26,792
"Your Allah, the Almighty and the Glorious,
has the glory above all of the men.

962
02:17:27,241 --> 02:17:31,721
Peace be upon You, O Prophets...

963
02:17:32,104 --> 02:17:39,714
Praises are only to Allah, the Lord,
creator, teacher and tamer of the realms. Al- Fatihah.

964
02:17:57,800 --> 02:18:00,840
- May Allah be upon you.
- Thank you.

965
02:18:02,197 --> 02:18:05,037
Every time before he slept..

966
02:18:07,938 --> 02:18:10,238
he would pray.

967
02:18:13,755 --> 02:18:17,515
He'd get angry with me when
I pray with a mistake.

968
02:18:19,116 --> 02:18:20,906
Yes.

969
02:18:23,549 --> 02:18:25,849
He wanted me to be
alim. ( Islamic scholar.)

970
02:18:27,351 --> 02:18:29,591
Yes, he did.

971
02:18:31,154 --> 02:18:36,874
You used to read so much.
He'd ask you questions...

972
02:18:37,207 --> 02:18:39,577
then he'd be proud of you.

973
02:18:41,735 --> 02:18:43,835
We are still proud of you.

974
02:18:48,676 --> 02:18:50,046
However...

975
02:18:52,010 --> 02:18:54,420
he loved you the most.

976
02:18:59,528 --> 02:19:02,878
He called you "Kara Osmanım."

977
02:19:06,243 --> 02:19:09,513
I love you too.

978
02:19:17,469 --> 02:19:19,459
You do.

979
02:19:37,444 --> 02:19:39,644
You do, brother.

980
02:19:42,618 --> 02:19:45,008
My brother.

981
02:19:58,860 --> 02:20:01,080
My brothers.

982
02:20:13,634 --> 02:20:15,964
Sons.

983
02:20:16,798 --> 02:20:19,258
You tore my heart out.

984
02:20:19,825 --> 02:20:21,975
You tore my heart out.

985
02:20:23,074 --> 02:20:24,304
However...

986
02:20:25,913 --> 02:20:27,413
I wish...

987
02:20:28,766 --> 02:20:31,296
you said these words...

988
02:20:32,331 --> 02:20:35,081
when our Bey was alive.

989
02:20:40,888 --> 02:20:43,308
I wish...

990
02:20:46,652 --> 02:20:48,752
I wish...

991
02:21:14,119 --> 02:21:18,119
We were nearly of the same age...

992
02:21:19,172 --> 02:21:22,132
however...

993
02:21:23,514 --> 02:21:25,344
we were ignorant, he was wise.

994
02:21:27,444 --> 02:21:31,444
We were reckless...

995
02:21:31,960 --> 02:21:34,940
he was brave.

996
02:21:37,797 --> 02:21:39,547
We were lavish...

997
02:21:41,976 --> 02:21:43,926
he was generous.

998
02:21:44,882 --> 02:21:50,612
We were angry, he was wrathful.

999
02:21:53,061 --> 02:21:56,131
He was born to be a Bey.

1000
02:21:58,536 --> 02:22:04,266
The happiness that
my Allah gave to the Turk Beys...

1001
02:22:05,950 --> 02:22:07,960
was glowing in him.

1002
02:22:11,856 --> 02:22:14,316
My Bey...

1003
02:22:16,096 --> 02:22:18,786
My Ertuğrul Bey...

1004
02:23:29,581 --> 02:23:32,321
Selcan Mother.

1005
02:23:33,566 --> 02:23:36,476
Tell us about Ertuğrul Ghazi.

1006
02:23:42,472 --> 02:23:44,942
How?

1007
02:23:47,176 --> 02:23:50,416
Words aren't enough to tell about
such a Bey.

1008
02:23:54,824 --> 02:23:57,724
Words aren't enough.

1009
02:24:00,105 --> 02:24:02,085
My Bey...

1010
02:24:03,498 --> 02:24:06,498
he was light.

1011
02:24:08,112 --> 02:24:15,572
During the peace, he was
understanding and merciful.

1012
02:24:16,979 --> 02:24:22,779
During the war, he was like a lion.

1013
02:24:25,560 --> 02:24:31,300
Before and after he was Bey, he couldn't
have a moment of peace.

1014
02:24:36,305 --> 02:24:40,305
Firstly, for Kayı and then us.

1015
02:24:40,992 --> 02:24:42,912
He tried hard.

1016
02:24:48,171 --> 02:24:51,561
I was young and ignorant.

1017
02:24:53,569 --> 02:24:56,879
I caused him trouble.

1018
02:24:57,593 --> 02:24:59,863
May Allah forgive me.

1019
02:25:00,755 --> 02:25:03,225
May Allah forgive me.

1020
02:25:03,606 --> 02:25:07,166
I hope he gave me his blessings Inshallah.

1021
02:25:07,236 --> 02:25:11,236
He did.

1022
02:25:14,210 --> 02:25:16,190
Selcan Mother.

1023
02:25:16,570 --> 02:25:19,820
You became a
mother to his motherless children.

1024
02:25:20,088 --> 02:25:21,408
I did.

1025
02:25:21,997 --> 02:25:26,247
You even raised your brides
like your daughters.

1026
02:25:34,243 --> 02:25:36,903
We're grateful to you.

1027
02:25:40,579 --> 02:25:44,779
- So is Ertuğrul Bey.
- Inshallah.

1028
02:25:45,280 --> 02:25:50,830
He gave his blessings so that he
entrusted Osman to you.

1029
02:25:51,313 --> 02:25:53,693
He did.

1030
02:26:04,978 --> 02:26:11,058
- You are my mother, from now on.
- I'd die for you.

1031
02:26:21,637 --> 02:26:22,827
My Gonca.

1032
02:26:23,805 --> 02:26:28,075
My beautiful daughter.
You're my daughter too.

1033
02:26:29,751 --> 02:26:35,561
Come here.
I'm your mother too

1034
02:26:39,728 --> 02:26:41,748
My heart hurts.

1035
02:27:33,020 --> 02:27:34,870
My father.

1036
02:27:48,138 --> 02:27:50,228
My valiant father.

1037
02:27:53,883 --> 02:27:56,103
My brave father.

1038
02:27:59,543 --> 02:28:02,013
My Ghazi father.

1039
02:28:16,313 --> 02:28:19,063
I waited for you.

1040
02:28:23,714 --> 02:28:26,564
I waited for you.

1041
02:28:30,001 --> 02:28:32,541
I waited for you to come.

1042
02:28:38,668 --> 02:28:40,528
You came.

1043
02:28:46,690 --> 02:28:49,950
You came but...

1044
02:28:52,121 --> 02:28:54,181
you were sick.

1045
02:28:56,437 --> 02:28:58,587
You were so sick.

1046
02:29:00,547 --> 02:29:02,677
You hurt my heart.

1047
02:29:13,631 --> 02:29:14,931
Father.

1048
02:29:17,964 --> 02:29:20,754
My dear father.

1049
02:29:51,328 --> 02:29:53,118
My father...

1050
02:30:13,648 --> 02:30:16,708
How will we be worthy of you?

1051
02:30:19,098 --> 02:30:21,928
How will we thank you enough?

1052
02:30:24,706 --> 02:30:26,786
Tell me.

1053
02:30:35,163 --> 02:30:36,763
Tell me.

1054
02:30:47,873 --> 02:30:49,603
My Osman.

1055
02:31:00,778 --> 02:31:04,348
My Osman. I'd die for you.

1056
02:31:06,141 --> 02:31:09,241
I'd die for your tears.

1057
02:31:17,566 --> 02:31:22,106
It'll be a good funeral.
Don't worry.

1058
02:31:28,000 --> 02:31:31,010
My Sheikh's followers are coming too.

1059
02:31:37,608 --> 02:31:39,188
May Allah give them a long life.

1060
02:31:42,104 --> 02:31:44,304
May Allah give them a long life.

1061
02:31:47,621 --> 02:31:49,331
Allah...

1062
02:31:50,707 --> 02:31:53,117
took his loved man.

1063
02:31:55,155 --> 02:31:56,915
My Bala...

1064
02:32:00,664 --> 02:32:03,104
we should be patient.

1065
02:32:05,370 --> 02:32:07,320
Of course, my Osman.

1066
02:32:08,046 --> 02:32:10,656
Patience is what is true to the Muslim.

1067
02:32:13,412 --> 02:32:17,872
If you want to talk, I'm here.

1068
02:32:22,150 --> 02:32:24,360
I know, my Bala.

1069
02:32:24,896 --> 02:32:27,256
I know.

1070
02:32:28,670 --> 02:32:30,100
From now on...

1071
02:32:35,382 --> 02:32:37,352
from now on...

1072
02:32:39,518 --> 02:32:42,088
it's time to do the hardest thing.

1073
02:36:31,493 --> 02:36:33,533
Abdurrahman Ghazi.

1074
02:36:35,973 --> 02:36:38,253
Son.

1075
02:36:46,707 --> 02:36:51,707
He's gone, the Bey of Kayıs is gone.

1076
02:36:56,620 --> 02:37:00,620
Ghazi of the Ghazis is gone.

1077
02:37:18,782 --> 02:37:23,752
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)

1078
02:37:23,962 --> 02:37:27,962
La ilaha illallah!
(There is no deity but Allah!)

1079
02:37:28,177 --> 02:37:32,247
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)
- Allahu Akbar! (Allah is the greatest!)

1080
02:37:55,223 --> 02:37:59,223
None of us will be sad...

1081
02:37:59,995 --> 02:38:03,125
for our Bey is dead.

1082
02:38:04,281 --> 02:38:08,281
Every one of us will be Ertuğrul Ghazi.

1083
02:38:09,942 --> 02:38:14,612
We'll look at Kayı's matter like him!

1084
02:38:15,026 --> 02:38:19,306
We'll go on this way with
his faith.

1085
02:38:23,600 --> 02:38:25,000
Sons...

1086
02:38:25,269 --> 02:38:31,359
Ertuğrul Ghazi is dead.

1087
02:38:34,653 --> 02:38:40,813
He'll be taken to the Lord of the realms.

1088
02:38:41,350 --> 02:38:45,350
However, he left you something.

1089
02:38:47,062 --> 02:38:52,338
He left you the
dawah of righteousness...

1090
02:38:53,058 --> 02:38:58,748
that he had brought to you over mountains,
that he protected at the cost of his life...

1091
02:38:58,748 --> 02:39:04,352
that he gave it to you here in Söğüt
to carry it on.

1092
02:39:05,421 --> 02:39:07,661
The seed of a great state...

1093
02:39:08,339 --> 02:39:12,339
is the good news of a great state.

1094
02:39:13,601 --> 02:39:16,511
Protect it.

1095
02:39:16,814 --> 02:39:19,074
Protect it!

1096
02:39:19,892 --> 02:39:22,172
Protect it!

